cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these graphs, please cite them as below."
title: "R(5,20) >= 427 and R(5,21) >= 447: Ramsey graphs on 426 and 446 vertices"
version: "1.1"
authors:
  - family-names: Chrisbacher
    given-names: Peter J.
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "A graph on 426 vertices with no K5 and no independent set of size 20, and a graph on 446 vertices with no K5 and no independent set of size 21, improving the lower bounds for the Ramsey numbers R(5,20) from 426 to 427 and R(5,21) from 445 to 447 (best public bounds we could find as of 24 November 2026; the survey values are 424 and 441). Both are built by Theorem 3 of Xu, Shao and Radziszowski (2011) from Mathon's 384-vertex cubic-residue graph and graphs from B. D. McKay's lists, with common induced subgraphs of 18 and 20 vertices found by search under the full Theorem 3 condition (in both, every K4 of the common part has two vertices in each of the two parts). The clique side is checked directly by two independently written exact programs; the independent-set side follows from the theorem, whose hypotheses are machine-checked, and has also been searched directly by exact programs (finished for both graphs). Version 1.0 contained the 425-vertex graph for R(5,20) >= 426, which stays in the release as history."
keywords: [Ramsey numbers, lower bounds, graph construction]
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Xu
        given-names: Xiaodong
      - family-names: Shao
        given-names: Zehui
      - family-names: Radziszowski
        given-names: Stanislaw P.
    title: "More constructive lower bounds on classical Ramsey numbers"
    journal: "SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics"
    volume: 25
    year: 2011
    start: 394
    end: 400
